Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://kubeos.in/

Package: kubeos-cli
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, openssl, iproute2, kubeadm, kubectl, kubelet
Description: KubeOS node orchestration: first boot, certificates, routes, disk facts
 The commands that turn a freshly installed machine into a working KubeOS node and
 keep it one: node-setup/node-ready (first boot), kubeos-node-join and
 kubeos-node-standalone (membership), kubeos-cert-renew (the 365-day control-plane
 certificates), kubeos-pod-routes (cross-node pod routing), kubeos-disks-report
 (LVM facts for the dashboard) and kubeos-dashboard-install.
 .
 /etc/kubeos/kubeos.conf is a conffile: POD_CIDR and SERVICE_CIDR default to
 "auto" and node-setup records the ranges it actually used in
 /etc/kubeos/cluster-network.conf, which this package never ships or touches.
